DRAFT — NOT IN FORCE. This is a fill-in of the canonical Business Source License 1.1
for korvus, using the decisions in docs/decisions.md (D112, D117, D129). Counsel MUST
(1) verify the "Terms" section below against the official MariaDB BSL 1.1 text verbatim,
(2) finalise the bracketed [TBD] parameters, and (3) decide the open question noted at
the end, before any public release. When the public engine repo is created this file
becomes its top-level LICENSE (per docs/license/README.md §2.1).

Notes to counsel (remove before release):
  - Licensor = 더베이스 (The Base) — the owner's choice (2026-10-26). A 개인사업자 (sole
    proprietorship), not a 법인, so no liability shield. The proprietor's legal name, registration
    number and address are private (docs/license/entity.private.md) and kept out of this public
    LICENSE. RECOMMENDED (counsel/owner confirm): (1) contact = a role address on the product domain,
    e.g. licensing@korvus.dev, not a personal gmail; (2) put NO governing-law/venue clause in this
    public BSL — the canonical BSL has none and most OSS licenses omit it; place governing law (Korean
    law) and dispute resolution (arbitration — KCAB in Seoul, or SIAC for international counterparties)
    in the separate COMMERCIAL license agreement instead; (3) if the proprietor must be named, use the
    English name "Trevor Kang"; "The Base" is a rendering of 더베이스 — confirm it is the intended
    English name or keep the 상호 with a parenthetical. (korvus / bauta stay brand names; Trevor Kang is
    the author, not the Licensor.)
  - The business reg. number, DOB and address from the certificate are PRIVATE and must NOT appear in
    this (public) LICENSE — they live in docs/license/entity.private.md for contracts/invoices only.
  - "Licensed Work" is versioned: each released version carries its own Change Date
    (release date + 3 years). A LICENSE stanza is added per version, or the template is
    parameterised so the build stamps the version + date at release.
  - Additional Use Grant is scale-based + self-attested (D129) AND bars offering korvus as a
    hosted/managed service at any revenue (D132). Counsel: refine the exact scope of "hosted or
    managed service" in clause (b) — the intent is to catch reselling korvus itself as a service
    (e.g. a cloud-browser provider), not to catch embedding the engine inside a product that does
    something else.

